Package: MultiSynSurr
Type: Package
Title: Synthetic Surrogate Regression with Several Synthetic Phenotypes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Haoyu", "Yang", email = "haoyuyang@hsph.harvard.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Association testing for a partially measured outcome (for example a
    metabolite measured on only some participants) that borrows strength from
    one or more synthetic phenotypes: predictions of the outcome from different
    sets of surrogates, each available on its own subset of participants. The
    outcome and the synthetic phenotypes are regressed jointly on a common design
    as separate outcomes of a multivariate normal model with missingness in every
    outcome (MultiSynSurr), extending synthetic surrogate (SynSurr) analysis
    (McCaw et al. 2024, Nature Genetics 56:1527-1536) to several synthetic
    phenotypes. Coefficients are estimated by generalised least squares given the
    residual covariance, which is estimated by profile maximum likelihood with a
    finite-sample correction; inference on the outcome does not depend on the
    accuracy of the synthetic phenotypes.
